// This file contains game-defined background descriptions
// Must start at 1000

{1000}{No significant background 

Nothing of any consequence has ever happened to the character. You start with 600 gold.}

{1001}{Raised by Snake Handlers 

You receive a 20% increase in your resistance to poison, but suffer a penalty to your Beauty (-1) due to the large numbers of bite scars on your arms and legs. You start with 700 gold.}

{1002}{Apprenticed to a Blacksmith

Your master is a hard man. You gain a bonus to Strength (+1) and a bonus to your Repair skill but you suffer a penalty to Dexterity (-2) due to the strenuous and repetitive hard labor. You start with 1000 gold.}

{1003}{Raised by Elves

You start with a wonderful suit of magickal elven chain mail, but suffer a slight penalty to all Tech skills. You start with 600 gold.}

{1004}{Raised by Monks

Piety has its advantages and disadvantages. You gain a bonus to Perception (+1) but renouncing the material world leaves you with only one quarter of the normal starting wealth - 150 gold.}

{1005}{Child of a Hero

You start with your father's +1 sword and are known throughout the land as a child of a Hero. Therefore you will incur terrible negative reaction for any evil act. You start with 700 gold.}

{1006}{Inheritance

You were orphaned as a young child and inherited a lot of money. The easy life has cost you a penalty to Willpower (-1). Most of the money has been spent by now, but you begin with twice the normal starting wealth - 1200 gold.}

{1007}{Foppish Elf

Raised in the city, you lose the elven bonus to dexterity but gains a bonus to Persuasion. You start with 600 gold.}

{1008}{Clanless Dwarf

Your parents did not belong to a clan, and would not discuss the reasons why. You gain no dwarven bonus to Tech skills, but you do start with an excellent dwarven war hammer. You start with 600 gold.}

{1009}{Disenfranchised Gnome

You are not part of the gnomish capitalist bourgeoisie and instead grew up as a day laborer. You suffer a penalty to Haggle, but gain a bonus to Strength (+1). You start with 400 gold.}

{1010}{Halfling Orphan

Abandoned in a large city as a child, you survived by stealing and never received any education. You gain a bonus to Pick Pocket, but lose a point to Intelligence (-1). You start with 600 gold.}

{1011}{Special Person

You have suffered congenital brain damage. You lack Intelligence (-2), but you receive more praise when you do good deeds (resulting in a better reaction from people). You start with 800 gold.}

{1012}{Professional Knife Tosser

You used to work as a knife thrower in a circus, until losing an eye in a freak accident. Sadly, you lose a point to Perception (-1), but you gain an exceptional bonus to your Throwing skill. You start with 600 gold.}

{1013}{Apprenticed to a Shopkeeper

Spending your whole childhood inside a shop, you gain an exceptional bonus to Haggle and some extra gold (800 gold), but you suffer a penalty to Dexterity (-1).}

{1014}{Sent To Charm School

Instead of a general education, you were sent to charm school. You gain bonuses to both Beauty (+1) and Charisma (+2), but you lose points in both Intelligence (-1) and Strength (-2). You start with 1000 gold.}

{1015}{Born Under a Sign

You were born during an astronomical event. As a result, you experience fewer critical hits and critical misses, but when you do get them, their results tend to be spectacular. You start with 600 gold.}

{1016}{Extreme Personality

You possess an extreme personality. People react more strongly to your presence, and tend to grow to either love or hate you. You start with 600 gold.}

{1017}{Factory Escapee

You were a slave in a factory until a recent escape. You have little money - 200 gold - but you gain a bonus to Strength (+1).}

{1018}{Freed Bodyguard

Your gnomish master recently died, and in his will you were freed from servitude, as well as being left a small monetary gift of 1000 gold. However, you are not very bright, and suffer a penalty to your Intelligence (-1).}

{1019}{Bookworm

You have spent most of your life reading. You gain a bonus to Intelligence (+1). Unfortunately, myopia has set in, and you lose a point to Perception (-1). You start with 600 gold.}

{1020}{Bully

You were the class bully, big and dumb. Extortion and intimidation have afforded you a bonus to Strength (+1), but getting people to do your homework for you leaves you with a deficiency in Intelligence (-1). You start with 600 gold.}

{1021}{Wild Half-Ogre

You were born to an ogre mother and lived with an ogre clan until very recently. Compared to your more civilized brethren, you gain a bonus to Willpower (+1) but you suffer a penalty to your Charisma (-1). You start with 600 gold.}

{1022}{Rare Half-Ogre Birth

You were born to a human mother, who miraculously survived your birth. Having been raised in the city, you gain a considerable bonus to Intelligence (+2). City life has also lessened your ferocity, and you lose points in both Strength (-1) and Constitution (-1). You start with 600 gold.}

{1023}{Suppressed Orcish Looks

You do not really look very orcish, but you are exceptionally surly. You have a bonus to Beauty (+2), but suffer a penalty to your Charisma (-2). You start with 900 gold.}

{1024}{Elven Blood

Your father's great-grandmother was an elf. You gain an increase in Magickal Aptitude (5%), but suffer a slight penalty to all Tech skills. You start with 600 gold.}

{1025}{Hyperactive

You are constantly busy. Your Speed is higher than normal (+1), but most people find you annoying, and your Charisma suffers (-1). You start with 600 gold.}

{1026}{Army Training

You received some army training during your youth, but were discharged for having flat feet. You gain bonuses to Strength (+1), as well as slight bonuses to your Bow and Melee skills, but you have a penalty to Dexterity (-1). You start with 600 gold.}

{1027}{Tough Hide

You were born with thick, brutish skin. Although you resist damage more than the average bloke does (10%), you unfortunately take a penalty to Beauty (-1). You start with 400 gold.}

{1028}{Sheltered Childhood

Your were cooed and coddled incessantly as a child. As a result of overprotective parenting, you take a severe penalty to strength (-6), but, being more sensitive, you have bonuses to Intelligence (+2), Willpower (+2), and Perception (+1). You start with 800 gold.}

{1029}{Troll Offspring

The gods frowned upon you when you were born. Cursed with both trollish looks and mannerisms, you receive severe penalties to Beauty (-4) and Charisma (-4). As everyone seems to think that you are spawned from monsters or worse, you often find yourself fending off hunters and holy men, and gain bonuses to Strength (+2), Constitution (+2), and Dexterity (+1). You start with 800 gold.}

{1030}{Ran Away with the Circus

Having run away with a local troupe of circus performers, you have gained considerable physical Strength (+6), but have serious deficiencies in Intelligence (-2), Willpower (-3), and Perception (-1) due to all of the schooling that you missed. You start with 600 gold.}

{1031}{Raised in the Pits

Being a veteran in the local pit fights, you gain a bonus to Strength (+2), Dexterity (+2) and a bonus to all Combat Skills. The vicious combat has also taken a toll. Head trauma gives you a severe penalty to Intelligence (-6). As a result, you're not especially good with money. Your entire life savings amounts to a measly 200 gold.}

{1032}{Feral Child

As an infant, your parents abandoned you in the middle of the forest. Having been raised by a pack of wolves gives you a considerable bonus to Dexterity (+3) as well as bonuses in the Skills of Prowling and Dodge. But, oblivious of table manners and the rules of good society, you receive a severe penalty to Intelligence (-6) as well as penalties in the Social Skills of Persuasion and Haggle. You begin with half the normal starting wealth - 300 gold.}

{1033}{Sickly

Mother Nature can be a harsh mistress. Having been born with an extremely weak immune system, you have penalties to Strength (-2) Constitution (-4), and Dexterity (-1). But all is not lost. Afternoons spent with a fever and a good book have afforded you unnaturally high Intelligence (+6). You start with 900 gold.}

{1034}{Beat with an Ugly Stick

You are ugly. There is just no other word for it, unless you consider hideous a better word. Children flee from you in terror and even the kindest of souls finds it difficult to stand your presence for long. As a result of your countenance, you take an extreme penalty to Beauty (-6), but, because you have had to defend yourself from frequent attacks, you gain a bonus to Strength (+2), Dexterity (+2) and a slight bonus to all of your Combat Skills. You start with 300 gold.}

{1035}{Lady's Man

Women swoon whenever they are near you. Being unusually good-looking, you gain a large bonus to Beauty (+6). Unfortunately, all that primping and powdering has you lacking in the more manly virtues. You lose points in Constitution (-2), Strength (-2) and Dexterity (-2). You start with 1200 gold.}

{1036}{Debutante

Your family is one of the most influential in all of Arcanum. As a young debutante, you have bonuses to Beauty (+3) and Charisma (+3). Of course, the easy life has made you soft in mind and body. You have penalties in Strength (-1), Dexterity (-1), and all of your Combat Skills. You start with 300 gold.}

{1037}{Raised by Orcs

You were a runaway orphan, homeless and starving, when an orcish family in the wilderness took you in and raised you. Their brutish ways have left you with increased Strength (+2) and Perception (+2), as well as given you a slight bonus to all Combat Skills. Unfortunately, your upbringing has also taken its toll on your personality, and you have a severe penalty to Charisma (-6). You start with 600 gold.}

{1038}{Charlatan's Protege

Having been convinced by a travelling salesman to become his apprentice, you've given up your life in the military academy you were enrolled in. You gain a major bonus to Charisma (+6), but lose some physical Strength (-2), Constitution (-2) as well as taking slight penalties to all of your Combat Skills. You start with 300 gold.}

{1039}{Merwin Tumblebrook

	Merwin Tumblebrook was raised in a small halfling town, where he showed a proficiency in various technological disciplines, but was also prone to random acts of theft and pilfery. Although not an evil child, his dresser was often full of the ill-gotten possessions of his friends and neighbors, as well as the occasional gold-leafed religious relic from a temple in the nearby human village. When young Merwin's tastes began drifting to explosives and the contents of the local treasury, his parents thought it time to take action.
	Merwin has boarded the IFS Zephyr en route to Tarant, where he is enrolled in the spring semester at the Westrel Military Academy for Promising Young Men. Needless to say, he is less than exuberant over the whole affair.}

{1040}{Godfrey Castleburger

	Godfrey Castleburger grew up on the rolling hills of his family's estate. The son of a wealthy and influential businessman, Godfrey was tutored daily by the best teachers, and excelled in economics and the dialectic method. In his free time, he was trained by a master in the technological discipline of Gunsmithy, and is well trained in the making of firearms and hopes to become an expert marksman.
	Having finished his compulsory education, young Godfrey is being sent to Tarant on the IFS Zephyr to broaden his experience in the new world, as well as to sow any of his proverbial wild oats before he returns to assume control of the family business.}

{1041}{Horace McGinley

	Horace McGinley was born under a bad sign. An orphan from birth, he found himself in a daily battle with life and its peculiar quandaries. After running away from various homes and institutions, Horace found himself on the streets, homeless and hungry. Carving a niche for oneself in such an environment is difficult, but Horace was anything if not determined. After falling in with a group of local street toughs, Horace began to learn the ways of combat and thievery, and even began dabbling in the ways of magick.
	With the money from a few successful heists, Horace has booked passage on the IFS Zephyr to Tarant. It's not that life won't give you anything, he thinks, it's just all in the way that you ask.}

{1042}{Muck Evil Eye

	Muck Evil Eye was born in a remote ogre village, the offspring of an unusual union between a human male and Histreg Wide Thighs, an ogre female whose appetites tended toward the exotic. Muck grew up an outcast, scorned by his fellow ogre because of his human heritage. He frequently found himself fighting because of aspersions cast at his family and his character; in time, he became the most feared, if not the most despised, warrior in his village.
	Muck, because of his human blood, is a tad smarter than the common ogre. Upon hearing of employment opportunities in the new world for half-ogre bodyguards, he's taken a job in the boiler room of the IFS Zephyr in exchange for passage to Tarant.}

{1043}{D'ren Le'lor

	D'ren Le'lor is a dreamer. The son of an elven hunter, D'ren found himself more interested in the history of Arcanum than he did in bowmanship, although he was quite proficient in the latter as well, and was often found in the library, poring over the ancient texts and manuscripts. Magick came easily to him, and he spent much time studying the ancient runes while his friends were off engaging in contests of physical skill and horseplay.
	To D'ren the world is a large and wonderful place. So tonight, after leaving a heartfelt note to his parents saying he would return soon, he has stolen away to the nearest town, where he's booked passage on the IFS Zephyr, bound for Tarant at first light.}

{1044}{Solomon Doone

	Solomon Doone was born the 13th son of Derzin Doone, the most evil necromancer in a long line of evil necromancers. It was the night of the full moon, and Solomon's mother, a frightful witch whose body was covered in strange birthmarks of the most evil shapes and configurations, died in childbirth at the stroke of midnight. Bezzle Gerts, the twisted, one-armed midwife who delivered the child, remarked that Fergel, the Doone's black housecat, had crossed the threshold into the room just as Solomon uttered his first cry.
	Oftentimes Fate is not subtle. After a family dispute that left most of the Doone clan unrecognizable or immobilized, Solomon has purchased a ticket for Tarant on the IFS Zephyr. He doesn't bother looking at the seat number.}

{1045}{Merik Luggerton

	The story of Merik Luggerton is not an unfamiliar one. Born into abject poverty, Merik lived with his family in a one-room shanty, working at odd jobs in the factory district of the city in which he lived. Orcish wages being what they were, the family had a lot of trouble putting food on the table.
	As in many orcish ghettos, there was a great demand for pugilists, and many were the men who placed bets on the outcome of a brawl between two strapping young half-orcs. Merik found himself in the ring one night, and, upon winning, had more than a month's wages.
	Merik fought, and Merik won. Having taken care of his family, he's purchased a ticket for the IFS Zephyr, in hopes of finding a new and better life in the great city of Tarant.}

{1046}{Lugard Bloodstone

	Lugard Bloodstone is a miner's son, and over the front door of his home is a plaque that reads: Any Work Not Done With Your Hands Is No Such Thing. Unfortunately, as a child Lugard seemed to excel at what his father dubbed 'senseless tinkering', and a young Lugard's birthday gift to his father of a steam-powered shovel went over like stone shoes at the swimming hole. Still, regardless of his father, Lugard studied long and hard, and looked to the day when he might study among the great inventors and scientists of Tarant.
	Lugard's father is old-fashioned, but he is also wise. Upon completing the dwarven rights of adulthood, Lugard has been permitted to enroll at Tarant University, and he's booked passage on the IFS Zephyr, bound for the greatest industrial city in all of Arcanum.}

{1047}{Victoria Warrington

	Victoria Warrington was the daughter of nobility, one of the lesser families who lost both land and power in the aftermath of the great wars. As the years have passed, the Warrington name has come to mean less and less, but the family has survived, and holds on to as much of its past glory as society will permit. Victoria is the youngest of three daughters, beautiful and quick-witted. Having been educated in the finest schools of knowledge and magick, she is the model of strong character and good breeding.
	But Victoria craves adventure. Many nights, she frequents the local taverns in disguise, hungry for stories, a strong glass of ale, and a game of dice. Tonight she's been lucky, and the poor soul across from her has lost his last remaining possession...a ticket on the IFS Zephyr to Tarant...}

{1048}{Bel'an T'Seraa

	The T'Seraa family name is an old one, and Bel'an has been raised with one standard: elven honor above all. She has been taught the true elven ways from birth, and holds them in her heart like a gemstone. Magick and warcraft are as familiar to her as the sun through the leaves of her treetop home, and she feels a strong kinship with Nature and Her mysteries...
	But all is not right in Arcanum, and Bel'an has been chosen by her people to go out into the world, and see what is to be seen. And although her heart breaks to leave the deep elven forests she has always known, there is a peculiar excitement she feels at boarding this...airship?...the IFS Zephyr, and traveling to someplace called Tarant...}

{1049}{Clarisse Vorak

	Until a little while ago, Clarisse Vorak had a bright future. Having recently moved to the city from a small town, she had apprenticed herself to a well-respected doctor and was well on her way to earning advanced degrees in the Anatomical and Therapeutic disciplines. She was a gifted student, and a quick learner.
	That all changed when it was discovered that the small town she was from was actually an orcish tribe. Times and attitudes being what they are, she has been asked to leave her apprenticeship. All of her friends have abandoned her, and her landlord has evicted her on "social" grounds.
	In the hopes that the new world has shed such prejudices, she has purchased a ticket on the IFS Zephyr, bound for Tarant...}

{1050}{Ke'ree Melange

	Ke'ree Melange has always lived in two worlds. Her father was a human politician, and her mother an elven sorceress, and she has learned to be a little like them both. Having grown up in both elven villages and bustling cities, she has come to appreciate the powers of adaptation and persuasion. She has always excelled in everything she has done.
	Ke'ree also remembers arguments between her mother and father concerning the nature of magick and technology, and why one was better than the other. After studying them both, she has concluded that both have merit, and that each has its place. After all, she thinks, if you can't live in two worlds, then you're obviously trapped in one...
	Having come to that conclusion, this very afternoon she has purchased a ticket on the IFS Zephyr, bound for Tarant. If there is a new world, she wants to be in it...}

{1051}{Educator

You are a natural teacher. As you learn skill training, you can teach your followers the previous training step. So as an Expert, you can teach your followers as Apprentices, if they qualify. However, since you spend extra time with each follower, you cannot have as many as usual (-1 to maximum followers). You start with 600 gold.}

{1052}{Super Model

You are a stunningly gorgeous woman, and you have been pampered and coddled all of your life. You gain a tremendous bonus to Beauty (+6) at the cost of Strength (-2) and Intelligence (-4). You start with 1200 gold.}

{1053}{Escaped Lunatic

You have escaped from an insane asylum and stowed away aboard the IFS Zephyr. You are extremely resistant to damage (+25% to normal, fire, electrical, and poison resistance) but you have no money, you have stolen some cheap clothing, and most people are frightened or repulsed by you (-25 reaction).}

{1054}{Idiot Savant

You were institutionalized at a young age and believed to be mentally handicapped. After several years, the institute lost funding and you were turned out onto the street. You are brilliant with a keen grasp of numbers and mathematics, but you are barely able to talk. You gain a significant bonus to Intelligence (+6) and an exceptional bonus to your Gambling skill and some extra coin - 1000 gold. However, years of being locked away makes you suffer physically and emotionally. You talk as if you had a much lower Intelligence and you suffer penalties to Strength (-1), Constitution (-1), Dexterity (-2) and Willpower (-2).}

{1055}{Tomboy

As a little girl, you were always playing games with the boys. As a woman, you can hold your own against any man, and you have avoided the stereotypical female role in society. This background negates the gender effect by increasing Strength (+1) while decreasing Constitution (-1). You start with 600 gold.}

{1056}{Barbarian

You were raised among a wild barbarian tribe in a far away land. No one knows how or why you came to be a passenger aboard the IFS Zephyr, but given your ferocious demeanor, no one tried to find out. You gain bonuses to Strength (+2) and Constitution (+1), and a slight bonus to Melee, while suffering penalties to Intelligence (-1) and Charisma (-2), and a penalty to Haggle. You also possess barbarian armor. You start with 600 gold.}

{1057}{Nietzsche Poster Child

Nietzsche once said "That which does not kill me makes me stronger", and he may have been referring to you. All your life you have been making mistakes, but you always seem to come out better afterwards. In other words, you critically fail more than normal but you have a 10% experience point bonus. You start with 800 gold.}

{1058}{Dark Elf Follower

You believe in the philosophy of the dark elves, that technology must be brought down at any cost. This faith has strengthened your resolve Willpower (+2), but the recent rise of technology has made you bitter Charisma (-2). You start with 600 gold.}

{1059}{Sold Your Soul

You have made a pact with a demon. In exchange for more magickal power, you have dedicated your life to the pursuit of evil. You gain 20% to Magickal Aptitude, but suffer -20 reaction from others and a -20 alignment (and your alignment can NEVER go higher). You start with 600 gold.}

{1060}{Day Mage

You were born with a magickal aptitude that has affinity for the sun. During the day (between the hours of 6 AM and 6 PM), you possess a 20% bonus to your Magickal Aptitude, but at night you suffer a 20% penalty to your Magickal Aptitude. You start with 600 gold.}

{1061}{Night Mage

You were born with a magickal aptitude that has affinity for the night. At night (between the hours of 6 PM and 6 AM), you possess a 20% bonus to your Magickal Aptitude, but during the day you suffer a 20% penalty to your Magickal Aptitude. You start with 600 gold.}

{1062}{Sky Mage

You were born with a magickal aptitude that has affinity for the open sky. While outside and in clear view of the sky, you possess a 20% bonus to Magickal Aptitude. But while underground, indoors, or even under a heavy forest canopy, you suffer a 20% penalty to your Magickal Aptitude. You start with 800 gold.}

{1063}{Nature Mage

You were born with a magickal aptitude that has affinity for nature. While standing on a natural surface, you possess a 20% bonus to Magickal Aptitude. But on a man-made surface, you suffer a 20% penalty to your Magickal Aptitude. You start with 800 gold.}

{1064}{Agoraphobic

You are terrified of open spaces. As a child, you rarely went outdoors and spent your time reading and studying, gaining a bonus to Intelligence (+2). You are fine if you are indoors or even in a thickly forested area, but if you go into an outdoor open area, you suffer a panic attack, losing your Intelligence bonus and leading to penalties in Dexterity (-2), Intelligence (-2) and Willpower (-2), but you do gain a bonus to Strength (+2) from the fear. You start with 800 gold.}

{1065}{Hydrophobic

You are deathly afraid of water and of drowning. As a child, you constantly made up reasons to avoid entering even shallow water, gaining a bonus to Persuasion. If you do find yourself in water, you suffer a panic attack, leading to penalties in Dexterity (-2), Intelligence (-2) and Willpower (-2), but you do gain a bonus to Strength (+2) from the fear. You start with 600 gold.}

{1066}{Afraid of the Dark

You cannot stand to be in the dark. You stay constantly aware of your surroundings, peering into dim corners and dark shadows to see if something is there. While this has raised your Perception (+2), you will suffer a panic attack if you are in too dark an area, leading to penalties in Dexterity (-2), Intelligence (-2) and Willpower (-2), but you do gain a bonus to Strength (+2) from the fear. You start with 900 gold.}

{1067}{Magick Allergy

You are severely allergic to magickal items, such that touching them causes you pain. Therefore, you have been devoted to technology since a young age and have developed a knack for it. You gain a +10% bonus to Technological Aptitude, but you cannot wield ANY magickal items. You start with 1200 gold.}

{1068}{Arsonist

You like fire. No, you LOVE fire! Fire! Fire! FIRE! You were always picked on as a kid for being scrawny, receiving penalties to Strength (-1) and Constitution (-1), but you showed them! You studied explosives, gaining +20 Expertise, and you burned their homes! Burned them to the ground! Ha ha! Then you ran away from home and snuck aboard the IFS Zephyr, which seemed highly flammable and an excellent target. You probably would have torched the zeppelin if it hadn't been shot down. You start with 900 gold.}

{1069}{Bandit

You are a gun-toting bandit. Your lifestyle has earned you a bonus to your Firearms skill, as well as a penalty to Charisma (-1). You ran afoul of the law and reached the IFS Zephyr just one step ahead of the authorities. You have your gun, some ammo, and only 300 gold.}

{1070}{Technophobia

You were raised on a potato farm in the rustic backwaters of a distant land. You worked hard, gaining a bonus to Strength (+1) and Constitution (+1), but you never experienced any technology of any kind. Subsequently, you are afraid of technological items and cannot bring yourself to even pick one up. You start with 400 gold.}

{1071}{Only Child

You grew up as the only child of very permissive parents, and you basically always got your own way. As an adult, you expect nothing less than total obedience of those around you, gaining a bonus to Willpower (+6), but your temperament leaves much to be desired, resulting in penalties to your Charisma (-4) and your Persuasion and Haggle skills. You start with only 200 gold.}

{1072}{Frankenstein Monster

You were reanimated by a mad scientist from various body parts he found at gravesites, but somehow you escaped from the laboratory. You are very well constructed, gaining bonuses to Strength (+4), Constitution (+4), Electrical Resistance (+30%) and Poison Resistance (+20%), but you have very slow Dexterity (-6), a damaged brain-larynx connection (you use dumb dialog options) and a susceptibility to fire, Fire Resistance (-20%). You also start out with only 150 gold.}

{1073}{Bride of Frankenstein

You were reanimated by a mad scientist to be the bride of his other creation, but somehow you managed to escape before the wedding. You are very well constructed, gaining bonuses to Beauty (+4), Constitution (+4), Electrical Resistance (+20%) and Poison Resistance (+10%), but you have a very slow Dexterity (-4), a damaged brain-larynx connection (you use dumb dialog options) and a susceptibility to fire, Fire Resistance (-10%). You also start out with only 50 gold.}

{1074}{Mad Doctor

You have performed numerous untested and dangerous medical experiments upon yourself and suffer from the adverse effects. You have bonuses to Intelligence (+2), Perception (+2), Poison Resistance (+20%) and Electrical Resistance (+20%), and a bonus to your Healing skill (+1), but you suffer penalties to Beauty (-1), Charisma (-1), Dexterity (-2) and Constitution (-3). You start with 900 gold.}

{1075}{Miracle Operation

Though born to a wealthy family as a young child, you mysteriously lost your sight. It was discovered that you had contracted a degenerative and always fatal disease. As a blind child, your early development favored indoor activities and development befitting the wealthiest of society. You gained bonuses to Intelligence (+3) and Charisma (+3). Your senses of touch, hearing and smell increased to compensate for your blindness, resulting in a bonus to Perception (+5). However, you suffered physically, leading to penalties in Strength (-3), Dexterity (-3) and Constitution (-5). As a young adult, your parents, out of desperation, paid for the services of a renown, if unorthodox physician, who miraculously restored your sight. You start with 1000 gold.}

{1076}{Dark Sight

Your eyes are overly sensitive to light. You are nearly blind in daylight, but you can see perfectly in darkness. Therefore, all skill lighting penalties are reversed for you. You start with 400 gold.}

{1077}{Clumsy 

Spilling drinks over clothing, tripping over your own laces, hitting the wrong switch and all other manner of careless blunders are your everyday run of the mill actions. Your parents tended to put you in a big chair with a book praying the chair would not fall apart and that the book would survive. You suffer a serious penalty to Dexterity (-4) and you have a greater chance of critical misses. However, you body has adapted to your own clumsiness and you resist damage better than normal people. You heal the wounds you get rather rapidly, reflected in a bonus to your Constitution (+3). All the reading you have managed to accomplish between the accidents also has had the benefit a bonus to your Intelligence (+2). You start with 400 gold.} 

{1078}{Gigolo Man

You are an incredibly good-looking man. Because you loved money, you "leased yourself" to ugly rich ladies. After a period of time a very jealous husband caught you on the act and beat the hell out of you. You manage to escape barely alive with one eye only and board the Zephyr. Because of the beating that you took from the jealous husband you now suffer a penalty of -4 in dexterity and -4 in constitution and -4 in perception. Amazingly, your incredible beauty did not suffer at all. Your charisma is also above average. You have bonus of +6 to Beauty and +3 to Charisma and 3/4 to your Persuasion skill. You start with 600 gold.}

{1079}{Son Of A Bitch

You are a son of an one-legged woman and pack of drunken sailors. Because of the starvation in your childhood you suffer penalty to your Strength (-2) and Constitution (-4) but you gain a bonus to your Dexterity (+2) and Pick Pocket skill (+1). Due to your frequent simulation of facial nerve paralysis (to cadge more money) you suffer a penalty to your Beauty (-2). As an experienced bastard and man without conscience you start with a magickal sword that you pickpocketed from someone known as the child of a hero. You also start with 400 gold.}

{1080}{Dwarven Handyman 

You were born weaker than any Dwarf in your small clan. To bring them no shame and to prove you worth you became the handyman of the small clan. You fixed the equipment, laid the traps against intruders, and opened the doors to whom the lock was stuck. The tedious work adversely effected your muscles even more. You suffer a significant penalty to Strength (-4) and a penalty to Dexterity (-2). However, you work and training in firearms, as you could not swing a weapon, results in a bonus to all your tech skills as well as bonus to your Intelligence (+3). You start with 400 gold.} 

{1081}{Assassin 

You are the blade in the shadows, the worst nightmare of royalty and nobility. You are a nefarious assassin. In your childhood you were always picked on by bullies, for you were physically weak, reflected in a penalty to Strength (-3) and Constitution (-3). However, getting yourself out of their grip did increase your dexterity and a taste for revenge. You have trained long hours and, after paying back their debt, you became a professional. Having recently completed a lucrative deal you are now heading for new grounds on board the IFS Zephyr. Your expertise gives you an exceptional bonus to your Backstab skill, as well as a bonus to Prowling and Spot Trap skills. Your profession has always urged you to nimbleness resulting in a amazing bonus to Dexterity (+5), but also made you rather cynical causing a penalty to Charisma (-2). Naturally you are an evil person, which is shown in a -10 to alignment (this can NEVER go higher). You start with 600 gold.} 

{1082}{Fugitive Con-Artist 

Lying is second nature to you. No, lying is your first nature! You can do nothing but lie and you scheme your way into everything. This has resulted in a tremendous bonus to your Persuasion skill, as well as bonuses in your Haggle and Gamble skills. You used your natural talent for lying to convince people to grant you access to high education, refined parties and their wealth. You gain a bonus to Intelligence (+2) and Charisma (+2). However, one noble did not take your actions well and hired a bounty hunter. Though you escaped this bounty hunter, he managed to throw a grenade which exploded in your face. This left you half-deaf and partially blinded, resulting in a severe penalty to your Perception (-6). You quickly talked yourself onto the IFS Zephyr. Even after your 'accident', you know you will never give up your ways (-10 to Alignment (and can NEVER go higher)). You also start with 600 gold.} 

{1083}{Veteran Gunsman 

You were a gunsman in the city guard until one day the Orcs that worked in the factory revolted. You answered the call of duty, but you got separated from your unit. Even though you did manage to gun down an Orc and wound another, they overwhelmed you. You woke up in the hospital and spend years recovering. Although you have managed to come on top of the event you remain scarred and walk with a limp. Thus your Beauty has suffered (-2) and you are slower than the average person (-2 to your Speed). You did retain a good portion of your gunsman training, resulting in a tremendous bonus to your Firearms skill and a bonus to your Perception (+2). You start with 400 gold.} 

{1084}{Female champion 

You are tired of being ignored and sometimes downright mocked by men. You know that you're just as good as a man - in fact, you're better! (+1 Strength, +2 Intelligence) You have devoted yourself to bettering the cause of female equality, and will defend it strongly (+1 Willpower). However, both men and women become annoyed with your unpopular viewpoints after they discover them (-4 Charisma). You start with 600 gold.}

{1085}{Chosen One

You believe that you are the Chosen One and one day you will be a great hero and save the world from a great danger. You bought a ticket to the airship in order to find your destiny. You have spent all your free time training in combat skills (+4/4 in every Combat skill and in Firearms). From all those years of training you get a bonus to your Strength (+1) and Willpower (+1). However, years of constant hysterical laughter from everybody around you have made you very bitter, resulting in a penalty to your Charisma (-6). You start with no gold, having spent it all on training.}

{1086}{Female Bodybuilder

From a small child you had a fascination with pure muscle strength. So you trained and trained until your body lost some of its agility (-1 to Dexterity) and a lot of its female beauty (-5 to Beauty). However you end up much stronger that the average woman - or the average man, for that matter (+4 to Strength). You start with 600 gold.}

{1087}{Fire Spell

When you were a small child you were trapped in a burning house with no way out. Your uncle, a powerful wizard, cast a spell on you to save your life, but you were badly scarred by the flames before it took effect. From now on you are almost immune to fire. You received a permanent 95% bonus to your Fire Resistance, but have a severe penalty to your Beauty (-4) and it can never be improved. You start with 600 gold.}

{1088}{Vampire

Your mother was bitten by a Vampire before your birth. After your birth she turned into a vampire and was killed by the local priest. However the priest did not detect signs of vampirism on you so he kept you as his own child. You learned the truth when signs of vampirism appeared on you. When that happened he tried to kill you but you were much faster than him. After that you swore to never drink blood again, resulting in an extreme penalty to your Constitution (can never be higher than 2). Most people also find something disturbing about you, resulting in a reaction penalty (-20) and a Charisma penalty (-1). Also, your fire resistance can never be more than zero. But you are faster than others; you get bonus to your Speed (+6). You also start with no gold because you escaped in a hurry.}

{1089}{Herbalist

You have studied to become a herbalist. You were reading herbalist books since a small child when the other children were playing. You gain +30 expertise in herbal science but permanently lose 8 fatigue points. You start with 600 gold.}

{1090}{Chemistry Scientist

You have studied to become a Chemist. You were reading chemistry books when you were a small child when the other children were playing. You gain +30 expertise in chemistry science but permanently lose 8 fatigue points. You start with 600 gold.}

{1091}{Electrical Scientist

You have studied to become a electrician. You were reading electricity books when you were a small child when the other children were playing. You gain +30 expertise in electrical science but permanently lose 8 fatigue points. You start with 600 gold.}

{1092}{Explosives Scientist

You have studied to become a explosives scientist. You were reading explosives books when you were a small child when the other children were playing. You gain +30 expertise in explosives but permanently lose 8 fatigue points. You start with 600 gold.}

{1093}{Gun Smithy Scientist

You have studied to become a gun smith. You were reading gun making books when you were a small child when the other children were playing. You gain +30 expertise in gun smithy science but permanently lose 8 fatigue points. You start with 600 gold.}

{1094}{Mechanics Scientist

You have studied to become a mechanics scientist. You were reading mechanics books when you were a small child when the other children were playing. You gain +30 expertise in mechanics science but permanently lose 8 fatigue points. You start with 600 gold.}

{1095}{ Smithy Scientist

You have studied to become a smithy. You were reading smithy books when you were a small child when the other children were playing. You gain +30 expertise in Smithy science but permanently loose 8 fatigue points. You start with 600 gold.}

{1096}{ Therapeutics Scientist

You have studied to become a Therapeutics scientist. You were reading therapeutics books when you were a small child when the other children were playing. You gain +30 expertise in therapeutics science but permanently lose 8 fatigue points. You start with 600 gold.}

{1097}{ Fragile bones

You are suffering from a terrible disease. Your bones are very fragile. Therefore you lose 50% of your hit points. To compensate for this and just to stay alive you have run all your life and thrown rocks at your enemies. You get a Speed increase of +6 and also a bonus (+6) to your Throwing skill. You start with 600 gold.}

{1098}{Dimensional Traveller

Arcanum is most certainly not your home. The mysterious experiments that brought you here have proven too difficult to repeat, and so you resolve to find a new life in this place. Your scientific past gives you +4 to Intelligence and +4 to Perception. On the other hand, Arcanum's strange culture and attitudes give you -6 to Charisma and, and a -10 reaction penalty (you look... odd, somehow). You don't have any local money but you start with a revolver and some bullets.}

{1099}{Tragic Doctor

You have been trained as a doctor. You get a large Healing skill bonus (12/4) and an Intelligence bonus (+4). You also get a bonus of 30 expertise in therapeutics and a bonus of 30 expertise in herbal sciences. Unfortunately one of your patients has died by your mistake. He was your only son. Your personality suffers tremendously as a result. Your willpower drops to 2 and can never go higher. You also get more critical failures in combat (+20 chance). You have donated all your money to the poor, so you start with nothing.}

{1100}{Mule

You could always carry more than other people of the same strength (+2000). But your speed is reduced by one. You start with 600 gold.}

{1101}{Gambling Addict 

All your life there has been nothing sweeter than the sound of dice rolling and of gold falling onto your lap. You always won big and always lost big. Whenever you were on top you spent money like there was no tomorrow gaining friends all over, but you never knew when to stop and always lost a lot again. Now you have boarded the IFS Zephyr for Tarant to look for new games and bets. Your lifestyle has earned you a tremendous bonus to your gambling skill, and your critical hits and misses tend to be pretty significant. Your socialising with every person around has gained you a bonus to Charisma (+2), but you clearly lack the strength of will to stop the addiction, reflected in a penalty to Willpower (-2). You start with 400 gold.} 

{1102}{Negotiator

You are very skilled in languages. You gain a large bonus to your Persuasion skill (6/4) and also a bonus to your Haggle skill (2/4). From selling many books, you start with double the normal starting wealth (1200 gold). However, since you talk so much with people, you don't have time for everyone (-1 to maximum followers).}

{1103}{Halfling Hunter 

You loved to skip classes in order to roam in the big world. You felt on top of the world when skipping small rocks across the water, fishing and exploring new terrain. As you grew up you became the village hunter, making sure there was meat on the table during festivals. You gain a bonus to your Throwing skill and a slight bonus to your Prowling skill. Your hunts have sharpened your skill and vision resulting in a bonus to your Dexterity (+2) and Perception (+1). However, skipping all those classes and little interaction with others have taken their toll. You suffer penalties to Intelligence (-2) and Charisma (-1). You start with 600 gold.} 

{1104}{Elven Ranger 

All Elves are one with the world and many devote lifetimes to the ways of Magic. You, however, were more interested in learning the fine art of swordplay and the expertise of the bow. As you reached adulthood you became one of the Elven Hunters. You were one of their best members until an encounter with human poachers let to violent struggle in which you were shot in the head and were left for dead. The Elven healers managed to bring you back from your coma, but the signs of the struggle are clearly visible. Your training gives you a bonus to your Melee and Bow skills, as well as a slight bonus to your Prowling skill. Training your body to those arts you also gain a bonus to your Dexterity (+3). Your injuries cause you to suffer penalties to Intelligence (-3) and Beauty (-2). You start with 600 gold.} 

{1105}{Gnome Hermit 

Though at first you were part of the Gnome bourgeoisie, you realised that this bred haughty and snobbish character. Disliking the way the Gnomes were becoming you turned away from the rich life to become a hermit. Your resolve in this matter grants you a bonus to Willpower (+3). Leading a less decadent life and hours of meditating have also granted small bonuses to Constitution (+1) and Perception (+1). However, for all that your lifestyle may be more healthy, the cold and harsh conditions have started to take its toll. This has lead to upcoming rheumatic joints, resulting in a penalty to you Dexterity (-3). You have also sworn off earthly wealth resulting in a penalty to Haggle and a quarter of the normal starting wealth (150 gold). After several years of contemplating you felt it was time to share your views with the other Gnomes and thus you boarded the IFS Zephyr towards the great city of Tarant.} 

{1106}{Gypsy Woman 

You were born to a gypsy family and made your livelihood by tarot reading, soothsaying and small magic performances. Although not every citizen believed in your visions you know the truth and they gave you insights that resulted in a bonus to Willpower (+2) and Perception (+2). You also receive a small bonus to your magical aptitude and your Haggle and Prowling skills. However, the life of a gypsy woman means you poured over the wisdom of the cards and missed out on physical training and education resulting in a penalty to Strength (-2) and Intelligence (-2). People also tend to dislike a gypsy no matter how warm your smile is. A vision led you to the action of boarding the IFS Zephyr bound for great city of Tarant with your gypsy fortune of 300 gold.} 

{1107}{Former Bodyguard 

You are the former bodyguard of a Gnome nobleman. You worked hard for him, saving his life on several occasions, and acting as brute muscle when needed. This has given you a bonus to your Melee and Dodge skills as well as slight bonuses to your Strength (+1), Constitution (+1) and Dexterity (+1). However, your employer never cared for proper medical treatment for your wounds resulting in a penalty to your Beauty (-2). Recently you have been replaced by a stronger and more docile Half-Ogre bodyguard leaving you rather vicious with the whole system. This has resulted in a penalty to your Charisma (-2). You start with 600 gold.} 

{1108}{Apprentice to Inventor 

You are the apprentice to an inventor. In trade for your tutelage you got all the nice jobs, like sweeping the floors, cleaning the lab and fixing all the broken stuff. This has resulted in an tremendous bonus to your Repair skill as well as a bonus to you Intelligence (+2). However, you are only known as the lowly apprentice and being cooped up in the lab all the day left you little opportunity for social interaction, resulting in a penalty to Charisma (-2). The fumes of the lab work have also taken its toll on your health. You suffer a penalty to Constitution (-2). You start with 600 gold.} 

{1109}{Amnesic Celebrity 

You have walked out of the wreckage that is the IFS Zephyr, but... you lost yourself. You can remember your name, luckily, but you can not remember what you did before all of this happened. Some vague memories about you being famous on another continent and wanting to make it in Tarant are all that come to your mind. It seems that many people also have vaguely heard of you, but unfortunately too vague to know exactly who you are. People in general react well to your sight and presence resulting in a +10 bonus to reaction and a bonus to Charisma (+2). However, the blow to your head has caused some damage and leaves you without a good drive and motivation, which means you suffer a penalty to Intelligence (-2) and Willpower (-2). You did find your well filled wallet among the wreckage; you start with 1200 gold.} 

{1110}{Tribal Demi-God 

You come from a barbaric region where Half-Ogres are very rare. You were the son of a barbarian mother whom was strong enough to survive the labor to give you birth. As you grew the tribe thought you a demi-god and that your mother had been blessed by a visit of their God of the Hunt. Demonstrating your strength the tribe soon worshipped you and you always got your way. This display of stamina and tribal command, supported by the wisdom of the elders, has resulted in a bonus to Strength (+2), Constitution (+1) and Willpower (+2), but made your demeanour all the worse causing you to have a penalty to Charisma (-4). When you mother suddenly became very ill she also became delirious and screamed out your were 'her living shame of her honor' as she had been raped. Broken hearted and driven away by the angry tribe, as you 'tricked' them, you left your homeland with little hope or money. You start with 150 gold.} 

{1111}{Social Worker 

You always had a soft spot for the less fortunate and you have made it your life's purpose to help these people. As a result people gladly listen to you and follow your advice. This results in a +10 to reaction and +1 extra follower. You also gain a +10 to Alignment (this can NEVER go lower). In your career you have always tried to take non-violent methods to solve problems and as such you are a true pacifist. This naturally leads to a penalty to in the lethal Bow, Melee and Firearms skills. These penalties would have affected your Dodge and Throw skills if it were not for the community ball games you frequently organised. You start with 600 gold.} 

{1112}{Holy Warrior 

You are a self-proclaimed Holy Warrior fighting all sorts of evil from Ogres to Thieves. Your righteous quest has taken you aboard the IFS Zephyr to the evil-infested city of Tarant. Your training gives you a slight bonus to your Strength (+1) and Melee skill. However, you have sworn off the less virtuous skills. Hence, the skills Backstab, Pick Pocket and Pick Lock all suffer a penalty. Your black and white view of the world strengthens your resolve resulting in a bonus to Willpower (+2), but leaves you with a rather strict perspective on the world causing a penalty to Perception (-2). This strict life also leads people to either applaud your efforts or see you as a fanatic. People therefore form more strong opinions about your person. Still you have a noble soul and therefore a +20 to alignment (this can NEVER go lower). You start with 6b00 gold.} 

{1113}{Ancient Blood

You have talked to many wise men and women, but none could give you the answer you seek. You know your blood is mixed with a powerful creature of old, but what kind of creature you do not know. Your blood could be anything; it may be draconic, it may be demonic or even angelic. You simply do not know. What you do know is that it leaves tell-tale signs. Besides of having exotic looks, you are stronger and hardier than most mortals resulting in bonuses to Strength (+2), Constitution (+2) and Beauty (+1). However, you have trouble controlling your strong emotions and you notice your perception of the world is tainted by your blood resulting in a penalty to Charisma (-2) and Perception (-3). Your blood also gives a small rise to your magical aptitude. You start with 600 gold.}

{1114}{Earthborn

You are one of the rare few Dwarves born every generation that is known as an Earthborn. All Dwarves have a connection with the earth, but you are 'One with the Stone'. Your unique connection causes you to have qualities like an earth elemental. You have the strength and stamina of earth resulting in bonuses to your Constitution (+4) and Strength (+2). Your mindset has become more firm, if slow to move. This results in a bonus to Willpower (+2), but a penalty to Charisma (-2). Your rough skin helps deflect blows, but results in a penalty to Beauty (-2). Due to this connection you do not share the natural affinity of Dwarves towards technology, as you are more focused on the earth itself. You lose all bonuses in the tech skills, and you actually gain a small magical aptitude. You start with 600 gold.}

{1115}{Panarii Acolyte

You were orphaned when your reached your early teens. Taking pity on you, the local Panarii priest took you in as his own. Here the foundations of your dream to become a Panarii priest were created. To complete your training you boarded the IFS Zephyr bound for the great city of Tarant and the Panarii temple in that great city. Your training as an acolyte has given you bonuses to your Willpower (+1), Perception (+1), Charisma (+1) and Heal skill. However, you have missed out the better part of regular education and you are unfamiliar with the value of gold resulting in a penalty to your Intelligence (-2) and a hefty penalty to your Haggle skill. You start with 600 gold.}

{1116}{Cosmopolitian

You were raised in a great city and as such you have been exposed to many cultures. You have learned how to sway each and everyone, resulting in bonuses to your Haggle and Persuasion skill. You have also learned to dodge the muggers, runaway carts and horsemen that crossed your path, resulting in a bonus to your Dodge skill. In many cities most of its inhabitants tend to work at jobs that require no manual labor and you are no exception. As such your muscles are not well trained, resulting in a penalty to your Strength (-2). You start with 600 gold.}

{1117}{Dwarven Activist

Unlike your Dwarven brethren, you believe the best way to help the humans understand the responsibility and power of technology is to to teach them. As such you have done the unthinkable and left your clan to go into the wild world to teach the humans. As you travelled you tried to persuade humans to give thought to their actions and created machines that were less damaging to the environment. These actions have resulted in bonuses to your Persuasion and Repair skills. Your resolve in the matter has given you a bonus to Willpower (+1). However, you did not participate in as much physical labor as many Dwarves do, and as such you miss the racial bonus to Strength. Trying to help the world is also costly and you start with half the normal wealth (300 gold).}

{1118}{Entrepreneur

Your life is about business. You invest money into projects in the hopes of reaping the benefits. Your latest deal seems to be the best as you board the investment, the IFS Zephyr. Part of this big air ship is built with your money and you are to get a percentage of its profits. Profits of which, a partial payment, has already reached your pockets. Your experience around the negotiation table gives you a bonus to your Haggle skill and a small bonus to your Persuasion skill. Your lifestyle has also given you a sharp mind and an aura of presence resulting in bonuses to your Intelligence (+1) and Charisma (+2). However, this also means you had a life in which you never strained a muscle resulting in penalties to Strength (-2) and Dexterity (-2). You start with 1200 gold.}

{1119}{Child of Fortune

You can not comprehend why the IFS Zephyr went down with you on board. After all, your vocabulary seems to miss the term bad luck. Everything always goes just the way you want it and your luck just never seems to run out. You are simply the pretty person with the luck of the gods. This is reflected in a bonus to your Beauty (+2) as well as bonuses to your Gambling and Dodge skills. When you strike a person your luck also comes into play giving you a much higher chance for a critical hit. Seeing you always got what you want without lifting a finger, you could never be bothered to care about your surroundings, your life, or what would happen, relying solely on your luck. This view on life is reflected by penalties to your Perception (-2) and Willpower (-3). You start with 900 gold.}

{1120}{Jack of All Trades

You originate from a small town where you did all kinds of jobs like militia, doctor's assistant and handyman. This has resulted in a variety of bonuses across a wide spectrum of skills like Melee, Dodge, Heal, Repair and Firearms, and attributes like Strength (+1), Dexterity (+1) and Intelligence (+1). In a sudden decisive mood you boarded the IFS Zephyr to go to the great city of Tarant in search of a new job. Many people from the village doubted you would succeed though as you simply were given those jobs because you never complained and were quickly pleased; which is reflected in a penalty to Willpower (-1) and Charisma (-3). You start with 600 gold.}

{1121}{Lonesome Traveller

Home is an alien concept for you; at best, the world is your home. You have travelled far and wide and always seek new places and ways to travel, as you deem the road just as important as the destination. Your experiences have given you a great bonus in Perception (+5) and the sometimes hardy conditions have given you a bonus to Constitution (+2) and Strength (+1). However, you are and remain a lonesome traveller and you rarely enjoy company. Thus, you travel with only one other person at most. You start with 600 gold.}

{1122}{Cursed Adventurer

You love danger and can not live without it. As such you easily took to the life of an adventurer and trained to become the best of the best. This training has resulted in a bonus to Dexterity (+5), Strength (+3) and Constitution (+2). Your hazardous experiences in the dungeons battling monsters and avoiding traps has honed your skills of Melee, Dodge, Bow, and Spot Traps, though it has left you scarred; reflected in a penalty to Beauty (-3). This, however, is nothing compared to the curse you incurred on your last trip. It caused your mind to become that of a beast resulting in a tremendous penalty to Intelligence (-6) and Charisma (-4). You were put on board the I.F.S. Zephyr by friends in hopes that a priest in Tarant might undo the curse. You start with 600 gold.} 
